# Nothing to copy here. Copy .env.template to .env instead, then fill it in.
#
# .env.template is the single source of truth for this project's environment:
# it documents every variable that main.py, database.py or compose.yml reads,
# which of them are required and which are optional with defaults. This file
# used to carry its own (partly stale) copy of the settings, the two copies
# contradicted each other, and that drift is what this refactor removed, so
# this file now deliberately lists nothing and cannot drift again.
#
# NEVER commit the real .env file: it is gitignored, and the templates are the
# only environment files that belong in git.
